      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "THE PROBLEM",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "estimated_duration_s": 22,
      "narration_text": "A single model call is one shot. Prompt in, answer out. It can't look something up partway through, run code, or notice its own mistake. Real tasks, like reconciling a report or fixing a bug, take many steps, and each step depends on what the last one found.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeWindow",
          "props": {
            "view": "artifact",
            "artifactTitle": "One call, one shot",
            "artifactHeading": "prompt in, answer out, no second look",
            "artifactLines": [
              "Can't look things up partway through",
              "Can't run code or call a tool",
              "Can't notice and fix its own mistake"
            ],
            "sparkLine": "Real tasks take more than one step."
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 17.13,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-11-18T20:59:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "THE MECHANISM",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "estimated_duration_s": 26,
      "narration_text": "An agent wraps the model in a loop. Given a goal, it plans a step, calls a tool, like a search, a database, or a code runner, reads what came back, and decides what to do next. It stops when the goal is met, or when it hits a limit you set. A model, tools, memory, and a stopping rule. That's an agent.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeWindow",
          "props": {
            "view": "artifact",
            "artifactTitle": "A model in a loop",
            "artifactHeading": "plan, act, observe, repeat",
            "artifactLines": [
              "Plan the next step toward a goal",
              "Act with a tool: search, query, run code",
              "Observe the result, then decide again"
            ],
            "sparkLine": "Model + tools + memory + a stopping rule."
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B02.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 19.11,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-11-18T20:59:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "THE LIMIT",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "estimated_duration_s": 24,
      "narration_text": "That loop is also the risk. Every step can build on an error, and an agent can confidently take ten wrong actions in a row. So the parts that must be exact, like money, identity, or anything you'd have to defend, still belong in deterministic code the agent calls, not in the agent's own guesses.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeWindow",
          "props": {
            "view": "artifact",
            "artifactTitle": "More autonomy, more ways to be wrong",
            "artifactHeading": "errors compound across steps",
            "artifactLines": [
              "Each step can build on a mistake",
              "Confident action is not correct action",
              "Keep the exact parts in deterministic tools"
            ],
            "sparkLine": "Let it act; don't let it guess the facts."
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B03.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 19.14,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-11-18T20:59:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "The verdict",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "estimated_duration_s": 16,
      "narration_text": "Before you trust an agent, ask four things. What tools can it call, and with what permissions? How does it know a step worked? When does it stop? And who checks the result? An agent is only as reliable as its tools, its checks, and its limits.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeVerdictArtifact",
          "props": {
            "artifactTitle": "Trust the loop, not the label",
            "artifactHeading": "An agent is only as good as its tools, checks and limits",
            "artifactLines": [
              "What tools can it call, with what permissions?",
              "How does it know a step worked?",
              "When does it stop?",
              "Who checks the final result?"
            ]
          },
